t; font-family:&quot;Calibri&quot;,sans-serif\">To summarize my understanding:&nbsp;</span></b><span style=\"font-size:11.0pt; font-family:&quot;Calibri&quot;,sans-serif\">your Delta UniForm (Iceberg V3) table sc_voc_rcp_txn writes some Parquet files whose footers are missing null_count statistics for the NOT NULL column RISK_SHAR_TRT_SBST. Snowflake, when validating the Iceberg table, treats the absent statistic as a possible null and rejects the file with &quot;non-nullable column without default has null values according to file statistics.&quot; Please correct me if I've misread any part of this.<br><br><b>To move quickly, could you help me with the following:</b><br><br><br></span></p><ol start=\"1\" type=\"1\" style=\"margin-top:0cm\"><li class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"text-autospace:none; word-break:break-all\"><span style=\"font-size:11.0pt; font-family:&quot;Calibri&quot;,sans-serif\">The Databricks Runtime (DBR) version(s) used to write the affected table, and whether the writes came from a job, notebook, or DLT/streaming pipeline.</span></li><li class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"text-autospace:none; word-break:break-all\"><span style=\"font-size:11.0pt; font-family:&quot;Calibri&quot;,sans-serif\">Consent to run debug commands on the table.</span></li><li class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"text-autospace:none; word-break:break-all\"><span style=\"font-size:11.0pt; font-family:&quot;Calibri&quot;,sans-serif\">Cluster url that can be used for testing.</span></li><li class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"text-autospace:none; word-break:break-all\"><span style=\"font-size:11.0pt; font-family:&quot;Calibri&quot;,sans-serif\">Confirmation of whether the same column definition and NOT NULL constraint existed at table creation, or was added/altered later.</span></li><li class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"text-autospace:none; word-break:break-all\"><span style=\"font-size:11.0pt; font-family:&quot;Calibri&quot;,sans-serif\">On the Snowflake side, it would help to know how you've configured Snowfl